I found one regression and one dependency verification gap in [PR #7](https://github.com/DarthMDev/pmd-sky-recomp/pull/7).

::code-comment{title="[P2] Give the runner binary a single build owner" body="The macOS and Linux presets use separate Ninja build directories from scripts/build.py, but both write to build/runner/nds_runner. After one build overwrites the other’s binary, Ninja can report “no work to do” and leave the wrong binary in place. I reproduced this with two CMake/Ninja build directories sharing one executable. An EU or dual-region build can therefore leave a preset launch using a runner with different ROM banks than the preset selected. Use one build directory for the shared output or keep the outputs separate." file="/Users/michael/projects/pmd-sky-recomp/CMakePresets.json" start=14 end=18 priority=2}

::code-comment{title="[P3] Verify the new ARM core pin on existing checkouts" body="The desktop build checks only that the dependency directories exist, then reports them as verified. A checkout from before this PR can still build against the old ARM core revision until the developer reruns setup_third_party.sh. The old local patch may make the build succeed, so the mismatch can go unnoticed. Verify the pin before accepting the existing checkout." file="/Users/michael/projects/pmd-sky-recomp/scripts/build.py" start=93 end=107 priority=3}

All 12 Python tests and 6 recompiler tests passed. macOS and Linux CI passed on `c351b8a`. Windows and iOS CI were still running when I checked.

